      "markdown": "## Parallel processing of products on the computer is\n\nParallel processing of pre-facilitated by a variant of (3) for computing C = AB, which is used by standard algorithms (such as in Lapack). In this method, A is used as given, B is taken in terms of its column vectors, and the product is computed columnwise; thus,\n\n $$ \\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{B}=\\mathbf{A}[\\mathbf{b}_{1}~\\mathbf{b}_{2}~\\ldots~\\mathbf{b}_{p}]=[\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{b}_{1}~\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{b}_{2}~\\ldots~\\mathbf{A}\\mathbf{b}_{p}]. $$ \n\nColumns of B are then assigned to different processors (individually or several to each processor), which simultaneously compute the columns of the product matrix  $ Ab_{1} $,  $ Ab_{2} $, etc.",
